    "status": "present",
    "value": "A directed graph is given as a list of edges [u, v], and every node has at most one outgoing edge. Starting from a given node, keep following outgoing edges until you reach a node that has none, and return that node; if the start node has no outgoing edge, return it. If the walk would visit a node twice (a cycle), return -1."
  },
